resources.string:
- Defining the app's colors, theme, and icons using Material2;


- Implementing the fragments that make up the app;


- Layouts built in XML, using DataBinding;


- Implementing the database (DB) for local storage to storage created notes. I used Room;


- Inserting Hilt as the dependency injection lib;


- Communication between fragments and DB made in the ViewModel and using coroutines;


- Implementing light and dark theme functionality;


- Transitioning fragments, using Navigation to navigate between fragments;


- Implemented the following features: deleting a note, updating it and checking it as finished;


- What a month, huh!

- Insertion of a splash screen, at this point, done with a dedicated activity;


- Another implemented feature: ordering notes;


- Layout adjustments after feedback received.

- Another major update of dependencies;


- Update and improvements of the use of coroutines in ViewModels and database;


- Start of screen migrations to Compose.

- Migration to the splash screen compat lib;


- End of Compose migration;


- Launch on Play Store with the app already in Compose.

- Migration from Material2 to Material3, updating colors and adjusting screens and components;


- Restructuring of project directories to follow Clean Architecture;


- Improving layouts and view logic in Compose, adopting the use of MVI.
